From 76a02f2df501035988c936b84719b3603296c92e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cruz <cruz@tbu.net>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 11:59:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 186/206] [vm] Shorebird: inline-dispatch FFI callback
 trampoline on arm64 (F155)

Restores upstream's pre-shrink shared stub layout (our ancestor
4679c040c63, before ec77e28f266 / 91cef061c78) on non-Fuchsia arm64 with
Shorebird's additions: per-FfiCallbackKind inline dispatch, inline
safepoint compare-and-swap with a slow path through
Thread::enter_safepoint_entry_point_, runtime-function table slots 1-3
filled. kNativeCallbackSharedStubSize 232 -> 560 (1978 trampolines per
page), kNativeCallbackTrampolineStackDelta 4 -> 2 with the marshaller and
simulator frame following. FfiCallbackTrampoline 16364 B on all three
fixtures, equal to theirs; sdk_phase_checklist C1 2 -> 0 (the last stub's
tail padding follows).

The thread.cc initialiser from this patch is dropped: F156/F157 already
sets enter_safepoint_entry_point_ (to SimulatorEnterSafepoint, where this
patch expected EnterSafepoint). Which value the FFI slow path needs at
runtime is NOT VERIFIED. Nothing here has run yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

